  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP for UNHAS operation in Sahel, 2014-2015</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian situation in and around Mali remains serious. According to UN 143,000 refugees is located in the neighboring countries and 86,000 are internally displaced. The security situation remains challenged, particularly in the northern part of the country, and the humanitarian needs are critical. UN&apos;s humanitarian air service, UNHAS, is indispensable in order to provide humanitarian and development actors access to northern Mali and to inaccessible areas in Mauritania and Niger. UNHAS&apos; aircrafts are used almost exclusively by employees of NGOs and UN organizations, and the service has transported 30,000 passengers to over 30 destinations in Mali, Niger and Mauritania in the first 11 months of 2014. The UN, however, has just appealed for additional funding, otherwise it will be necessary to cut routes and air services.</narrative>
  </description>
